---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '2026-05-03';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Terms governing use of The Automations Guide website and content."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" />
  </Fragment>

  <article class="container" style="max-width:760px;padding-top:3rem;padding-bottom:5rem;">
    <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
    <p style="color:var(--text-muted);">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <h2>Acceptance</h2>
    <p>
      By using theautomationsguide.com, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please
      don't use the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Editorial content</h2>
    <p>
      All content on this site reflects the personal opinions and experiences of the author at
      the time of writing. Tools change. Pricing changes. Vendor positioning changes. We try to
      keep things accurate but make no warranty that any specific recommendation will work in
      your situation.
    </p>
    <p>
      Nothing on this site is professional advice — legal, financial, technical, or otherwise.
      Test things in a non-production environment before deploying to your real GTM stack.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate relationships</h2>
    <p>
      Many recommended tools are linked via affiliate programs. See our
      <a href="/disclosure">Affiliate Disclosure</a> for details. Affiliate relationships do
      not influence which tools we recommend or how we describe them.
    </p>

    <h2>Trademarks</h2>
    <p>
      Tool names mentioned (HubSpot, Salesforce, Make, Zapier, n8n, Apollo, Clay, etc.) are
      trademarks of their respective owners. Use of these names is for editorial reference and
      does not imply endorsement by those companies.
    </p>

    <h2>Your content</h2>
    <p>
      If you submit comments, feedback, or other content (via email or other channels), you grant
      us a non-exclusive license to quote or reference that content in future articles. We'll
      anonymize personal details unless you explicitly grant permission to attribute.
    </p>

    <h2>Linking</h2>
    <p>
      Feel free to link to any page on this site. If you'd like to republish content (with
      attribution + link back), reach out — we usually say yes.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, The Automations Guide and its operator are not
      liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, or consequential damages arising from your
      use of the site or any tool recommended on it.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update these terms occasionally. Continued use of the site after updates constitutes
      acceptance of the revised terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:ian@theautomationsguide.com">ian@theautomationsguide.com</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
